From: AirPlay Controller local integration
Subject: [PATCH] airplay: preserve queued RTSP request ownership on connect failure

`evrtsp_make_request()` inserts the request into the connection queue before
attempting the socket connection. It retains that request even when the
immediate connection attempt returns an error. `sequence_continue()` then
freed the same request before deferred session cleanup walked the connection
queue, causing a deterministic use-after-free/SIGSEGV when an AirPlay 2 target
was temporarily unreachable.

Mark the request as transferred immediately after `evrtsp_make_request()`.
The deferred `session_free()` path then releases it exactly once with the rest
of the connection queue.

--- a/src/outputs/airplay.c
+++ b/src/outputs/airplay.c
@@ -3817,6 +3817,11 @@ sequence_continue(struct airplay_seq_ctx *seq_ctx)
   DPRINTF(E_DBG, L_AIRPLAY, "%s: Sending %s to '%s'\n", seq_ctx->log_caller, cur_request->name, session->devname);
 
   ret = evrtsp_make_request(session->ctrl, req, cur_request->rtsp_type, uri);
+  // evrtsp_make_request() queues the request before connecting and retains it
+  // even when the immediate connection attempt fails. The connection cleanup
+  // path now owns the request in both the success and failure cases.
+  req = NULL;
+
   if (ret < 0)
     goto error;
 
